---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { ADS, SITE } from '../config/site';
const updated = 'November 21, 2026';
// Once an AdSense publisher id is configured the advertising section is written in the present tense.
const adsLive = Boolean(ADS.client);
const email = SITE.contactEmail;
const siteUrl = Astro.site?.origin ?? '';
---
<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How SkillSprint handles information: game results stay in your browser, and how advertising partners such as Google use cookies."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  lead={`Last updated ${updated}`}
  narrow
>
  <p>This Privacy Policy explains what information SkillSprint (“SkillSprint”, “we”, “us”) collects when you use {siteUrl ? <a href={siteUrl}>{siteUrl.replace(/^https?:\/\//, '')}</a> : 'this website'}, how it is used, and the choices you have. If anything here is unclear, <a href="/contact/">contact us</a>.</p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You can play every game without an account. We never ask for your name or email address to play.</li>
    <li>Your scores, streaks and settings are saved in your own browser and are not sent to us.</li>
    <li>{adsLive ? 'We show ads from Google AdSense. Google and its partners may use cookies to show ads, including personalised ads where you allow it.' : 'We do not show ads yet. When we start, ads will come from Google AdSense, and Google and its partners may use cookies as described below.'}</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Information stored on your device</h2>
  <p>To remember your progress, SkillSprint uses your browser’s <strong>local storage</strong> to save, on your device only:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>personal best scores and a history of your recent results;</li>
    <li>daily challenge results and your streak;</li>
    <li>game settings you choose, such as test length or difficulty;</li>
    <li>your light or dark theme choice.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This data is read and written by the page running in your browser. It is not uploaded to our servers, not linked to your identity and not shared across devices. You can delete it at any time with “Reset all data” on <a href="/stats/">My stats</a>, or by clearing this site’s data in your browser settings.</p>

  <h2>Information you send us</h2>
  <p>If you contact us by email, we receive your email address and whatever you write. We use it only to reply to you and to fix any problem you report, and we delete it when it is no longer needed for that purpose.</p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>SkillSprint’s own code does not set cookies. {adsLive ? 'Our advertising partner, Google, sets and reads cookies and similar technologies on our pages, as explained in the next section.' : 'When advertising is switched on, our advertising partner Google will set and read cookies and similar technologies on our pages, as explained in the next section.'} You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings; the games keep working without them.</p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  {adsLive ? (
    <p>SkillSprint is free because it is supported by advertising. We use Google AdSense to show ads.</p>
  ) : (
    <p>SkillSprint is designed to be supported by advertising so that it can stay free. We do not show ads yet. When we do, they will be provided by Google AdSense, and the following will apply:</p>
  )}
  <ul>
    <li>Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this website or other websites.</li>
    <li>Google’s use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visit to this site and/or other sites on the Internet.</li>
    <li>You can opt out of personalised advertising by visiting Google’s <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener">Ads Settings</a>. You can also opt out of some other vendors’ use of cookies for personalised advertising at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a> or, in Europe, <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" rel="noopener">youronlinechoices.eu</a>.</li>
    <li>If you opt out, you will still see ads, but they will be less related to your interests.</li>
    <li>Visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland are asked for consent through a consent message before personalised ads are shown, and can change that choice at any time.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To learn how Google uses data when you use our site, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services</a>. Google’s own privacy policy is at <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.</p>

  <h2>Server logs</h2>
  <p>Like almost every website, the service that hosts SkillSprint may automatically record technical details when your browser requests a page, such as your IP address, browser type, the page requested and the time. This is used to keep the site secure and running, and is kept only as long as the hosting provider needs it for that purpose.</p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>SkillSprint does not currently use any analytics or tracking service. If we add one, we will update this policy first.</p>

  <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
  <p>SkillSprint is a general-audience website and is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has sent us personal information, contact us and we will delete it.</p>

  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR in Europe or the CCPA in California), you may have the right to access, correct or delete personal information about you, and to object to or limit how it is used. Because your game data never leaves your browser, you can view and delete it yourself on <a href="/stats/">My stats</a>. For emails you have sent us, or any other privacy request, <a href="/contact/">contact us</a>. For data used by Google for advertising, use the Google links above.</p>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>Some pages link to other websites, such as the sources of our flag and map data. Those websites have their own privacy policies.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy, for example when we add or change a service. The date at the top shows the latest version.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>{email ? <>Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> with any privacy question.</> : <>Questions about this policy can be sent using the details on our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</>}</p>
</PageLayout>
